  "statement": "Apply the Newton-Raphson method to $f(x)=x^{2}-5$ starting from $x_{0}=2$ to find $\\sqrt{5}$, and give $x_{1}$ and $x_{2}$.",
  "solution": "The iteration is $x_{n+1}=x_{n}-\\dfrac{x_{n}^{2}-5}{2x_{n}}=\\dfrac{x_{n}+5/x_{n}}{2}$. $x_{1}=\\tfrac{2+2.5}{2}=2.25$; $x_{2}=\\tfrac{2.25+5/2.25}{2}=\\tfrac{2.25+2.222\\ldots}{2}\\approx2.23611$. Already $x_{2}^{2}\\approx5.0000$.",
  "hints": [
    "Write the Newton-Raphson update for $x^{2}-5$.",
    "Compute two iterations from $x_{0}=2$."
  ],
